Test rg40 (XFAIL): ascii's NUL-padded last word lands on a used word -- must fail
// ascii packs two bytes per word, and the last word of a string whose bytes
// plus the NUL are odd is padded with a zero byte; that word must be marked
// too. "ab" is a, b, NUL:
// two words, of which the second, at 101, is the padded one. The control is
// rg15_ascii, and "abc" would fill its last word and always fail.
101/
    hlt
100/
    ascii "ab"
stop
